-- title:
--   The block product $\tfrac{1}{10!}Z_{10}\times\tfrac{1}{10!}Z_{10}$ of two dilated zonotopes in $\mathbb{R}^{20}$
-- statement:
--   Write a point of $\mathbb{R}^{20}$ as $x=(x',x'')$ with $x'=(x_1,\dots,x_{10})$ and $x''=(x_{11},\dots,x_{20})$, and let
--
--   $$Z_{10}=\sum_{i=1}^{10}\Bigl[-\tfrac{1}{2\cdot9!}e_i,\ \tfrac{1}{2\cdot9!}e_i\Bigr]+\Bigl[-\tfrac{1}{2\cdot9!}\mathbf 1,\ \tfrac{1}{2\cdot9!}\mathbf 1\Bigr]\subset\mathbb{R}^{10}$$
--
--   be the centered zonotope generated by the ten coordinate vectors and the diagonal $\mathbf 1=(1,\dots,1)$. The file defines the product zonotope
--
--   $$Z^\times=\Bigl\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{20}:\ x'\in\tfrac{1}{10!}Z_{10}\ \text{and}\ x''\in\tfrac{1}{10!}Z_{10}\Bigr\}=\tfrac{1}{10!}Z_{10}\times\tfrac{1}{10!}Z_{10}.$$
--
--   $Z^\times$ is a nonempty compact convex set, and its support function is
--
--   $$h_{Z^\times}(u)=\frac{\sum_i|u'_i|+\bigl|\sum_iu'_i\bigr|+\sum_i|u''_i|+\bigl|\sum_iu''_i\bigr|}{2\cdot9!\cdot10!}\qquad(u\in\mathbb{R}^{20}),$$
--
--   which is exactly the brightness function of the product $K=T_{10}\times T_{10}$ of two standard simplices. Consequently $Z^\times$ is the projection body of $K$, and its volume $121/\bigl((9!)^{20}(10!)^{20}\bigr)$ is the numerator of the normalized projection volume of $K$.
--
--   **Formalization Note** `productZonotope` is `splitBlocks ⁻¹' (((1 / 10!) • simplexZonotope 10) ×ˢ ((1 / 10!) • simplexZonotope 10))`, with the dilations taken as pointwise scalar multiples of sets.
